{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns","id":938575,"title":"Where should be the Rank 5 Caerns?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-27T21:14:27-07:00","id":938575,"title":"Where should be the Rank 5 Caerns?","content":"There should only be a few Rank 5 caerns around the world. Given that they are the only place one can learn Rank 5 Gifts at, they are very important to any chronicle. However, I have not liked the canonical Rank 5 caerns that I read about. They just didn't seem to make sense.<br /> <br /> The rank 5 caern at the Finger Lakes in New York. That seemed more like a rank 3 to me. There just doesn't seem to be enough actual history or myth to be a rank 5 caern of enigmas and healing.<br /> <br /> The rank 5 crossroads caern of that allows far greater travel is located in... Morocco? It is neither known to be an origin of discovery (that say just a little north in Spain around the port of Seville which was the origin of many voyages in the Age of Discovery) nor an actual crossroads of actual world trade (such as Samarkand along the Silk Road, the Straits of Malacca, the Syrian entrepot at the end of the Silk Road, or the Dardanelles).<br /> <br /> There is a rank 5 caern of Gnosis at the Qualla Boundary in western North Carolina. Again, I don't know anything about this region which would seem to be so full of spiritual wisdom or power. Instead, I would imagine an appropriate site would be more like the red rocks at Sedona, AZ where New Agers say &quot;energy vortexes&quot; and a &quot;spiritual power center&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that rank 5 caerns can only be at places in the real world which strongly correspond to the caern type. Fictional history or mythology can be an appropriate substitute. I'm not sure exactly where in the Urals the Sept of the Crescent Moon is at, but as the birthplace and capital of the Silver Fangs, it makes a perfect rank 5 caern of kingship.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I can imagine some places that would make sense as a site for a rank 5 caern, but there's nothing. Surely there is some kind of Rank 5 caern of plenty controlled by the Glass Walkers in London which was the financial center of the world for centuries, and capital of the world's largest empire for many decades. There are some very impressive mountains around the world where a rank 5 caern of stamina would make sense.<br /> <br /> So what do you think? How many rank 5 caerns should the world have. What are some good places they'd be located and what kind of caern should it be? We can talk about likely sept organization or tribal control.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> London<br /> Caern: The City of London, located in the Steelyard where the old London Kontor of the Hanseatic League was located; now a private bank office<br /> Level: 5<br /> Gauntlet: 2<br /> Type: Plenty<br /> Tribal Structure: Glass Walkers<br /> Totem: Silver Dragon<br /> <br /> The caern was established in the city of London in the Middle Ages when London first became an important commercial city and the Hanseatic League opened one of its kontore there. It was originally the outpost of German Glass Walker kinfolk from Lubeck which was also home to a caern of plenty. However, it did not become a Rank 5 caern until the late 17th century when the city became a worldwide center of commerce and finance. Ironically, it thrived while the Lubeck caern declined as the Baltic Sea trade became less important than the Atlantic. Despite the occasional problem with the British economy, the caern remains the foremost caern of plenty in the world, and is jealously controlled by the Glass Walkers whose kinfolk maintain cover for this urban caern as a luxurious private bank with worldwide clients among the elite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T21:42:27-07:00","id":938587,"title":"","content":"I always figured places that scream &quot;rank 5 caern&quot; would be quickly bulldozed by the minions of the wyrm and turned into a tire factory; So keeping them on the &quot;DL&quot; very important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:07:04-07:00","id":938625,"title":"","content":"Wait... when did Caern Rank have anything to do with what Gifts you can learn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:10:14-07:00","id":938628,"title":"","content":"Black.. Last i checkd you just needed someone OF rank 5 to teach you the gift, not a Caern of rank 5 to get it from..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T01:08:44-07:00","id":938678,"title":"","content":"And that's only if you take the rather extreme method of learning a Gift from another Garou instead of just summoning up a spirit that can teach the Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T03:30:02-07:00","id":938714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938625#post938625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... when did Caern Rank have anything to do with what Gifts you can learn?</div> </div> </div> </div>That echoes the WTF I just had. Carn Rank has nothing to do with available Gifts... Outside that, there should be exactly as many Rank 5 Caerns in the world as your plot requires. According to the books, they are not exactly rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T04:32:49-07:00","id":938730,"title":"","content":"Not true. Garou can teach garou gifts, but that is frowned upon. It also has the problem, that learning involves trail and error and is not at all the same as being bestowed a gift of a spirit. Just imagine you training to turn your claws into silver and something going wrong....<br /> <br /> <br /> W20 still has the old rule of thumb on page 151, reading:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Traditionally, the Garou first travels to a caern with a power level equal to or greater than that of the desired Gift to petition the spirit personally \u2014 to do otherwise is to defy tradition, which risks incurring the wrath of the spirit. </div> </div> </div>So, direct connection between gift level and caern level. Other revised sources indicate, that probably a mentor/Elder/Ritemaster at a sept with a lower level caern might summon a spirit so it can be petitioned for a gift. But in general a spirit capable of teaching a gift of level 5 will only roam in the vicinity of a level 5 caern (or deeper in the Umbra).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 07-28-2016, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T04:53:54-07:00","id":938737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns#post938575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rank 5 crossroads caern of that allows far greater travel is located in... Morocco? It is neither known to be an origin of discovery (that say just a little north in Spain around the port of Seville which was the origin of many voyages in the Age of Discovery) nor an actual crossroads of actual world trade (such as Samarkand along the Silk Road, the Straits of Malacca, the Syrian entrepot at the end of the Silk Road, or the Dardanelles).</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting wikipedia &quot;Casablanca is Morocco's chief <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port\" target=\"_blank\">port</a> and one of the largest <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_center\" target=\"_blank\">financial centers</a> on the African continent.&quot; and &quot;Casablanca is Morocco's chief <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port\" target=\"_blank\">port</a> and one of the largest <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_center\" target=\"_blank\">financial centers</a> on the African continent.&quot; Together with the port of Mohameddina 30km north, they perform 50% of the countrie's trade. Even in BC times, the city was influential for Phoenician and Roman sea travel. Having the mysterious Phat spirit housing his unique level 5 caern here, is okay, really.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:33:28-07:00","id":938932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938730#post938730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not true. Garou can teach garou gifts, but that is frowned upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point we were making is that if you want to learn a Rank 5 Gift from another Garou (despite the issues with that process) they need to be Rank 5 because they need to know that Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, direct connection between gift level and caern level. </div> </div> </div>Huh. Well there you go.<br /> <br /> I guess it's never mattered in any of my games because some combinations of:<br /> <br /> - The ST set it in/with easy access to a Rank 5 Caern in the first place to justify a large cast of characters<br /> - By the time higher Rank was achieved to qualify for such Gifts there was enough Umbra questing in the game that a lot of Gifts were earned in the appropriate Realms.<br /> - By the time higher Rank was achieved the group's Theurge/ritualist was good enough as Summoning themselves they could easily score enough successes to knock the impressions of a spirit that might be peeved about the Caern not being fitting up the chart enough it didn't matter.<br /> <br /> I think an additional issue is that the game doesn't actually set any factor on Gifts that makes higher Rank Gifts need &quot;better&quot; spirits. There's nothing to indicate that a level 1 Gift taught by Rat spirits, and a level 5 Gift taught by Rat spirits can't be taught by the exact same specific Rat spirit. Only specific Gifts explicitly state a stricter requirement (like calling for an Avatar of one of the Tribal Totems instead of just a spirit of that Totem's brood).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:57:33-07:00","id":938950,"title":"","content":"Prior to reading it in this thread, I had never heard of needing Caern rank to learn Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938932#post938932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it's never mattered in any of my games because some combinations of:<br /> <br /> - The ST set it in/with easy access to a Rank 5 Caern in the first place to justify a large cast of characters<br /> - By the time higher Rank was achieved to qualify for such Gifts there was enough Umbra questing in the game that a lot of Gifts were earned in the appropriate Realms.<br /> - By the time higher Rank was achieved the group's Theurge/ritualist was good enough as Summoning themselves they could easily score enough successes to knock the impressions of a spirit that might be peeved about the Caern not being fitting up the chart enough it didn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much these reasons for games I've played in or ran as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938932#post938932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an additional issue is that the game doesn't actually set any factor on Gifts that makes higher Rank Gifts need &quot;better&quot; spirits. There's nothing to indicate that a level 1 Gift taught by Rat spirits, and a level 5 Gift taught by Rat spirits can't be taught by the exact same specific Rat spirit. Only specific Gifts explicitly state a stricter requirement (like calling for an Avatar of one of the Tribal Totems instead of just a spirit of that Totem's brood).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this in theory. In my games though I tended to run the lower rank gifts being able to be taught by any spirit and around rank 3-4+ needing at least Jagglings to teach them (which are easy enough to find or summon). Nothing says its required but it made sense to me. I can't honestly think of a time it ever came up as a point of contention, so I guess it really didn't matter. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:34:35-07:00","id":939087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938587#post938587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always figured places that scream &quot;rank 5 caern&quot; would be quickly bulldozed by the minions of the wyrm and turned into a tire factory; So keeping them on the &quot;DL&quot; very important.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're generally too far off into the dark, goffic wilderness of the WoD to be seen regularly. And it's likely that if you see one and aren't a Garou, you're either likely to die, or a Zmei looking for a meal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:18:54-07:00","id":939129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939087#post939087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they're generally too far off into the dark, goffic wilderness of the WoD to be seen regularly. And it's likely that if you see one and aren't a Garou, you're either likely to die, or a Zmei looking for a meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this.<br /> So for me, level 5 caerns should generally be far out of the way. I only use a handful of them in my games and they are always hard to get to and well protected.<br /> I'd say there are only about 1-3 level 5 Caerns per continent, if that. None are left on the east coast of the US since the human populations are too high and I've had them closed, destroyed or corrupted during the expansion west.<br /> The level 5 Strider Caern (the Wheel of Ptah) doesn't really both me so much. The idea of the Glasswalkers having a level 5 Caern is kind of an odd thought though to me. I never considered any inner city Caern to be that powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:49:10-07:00","id":939260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938625#post938625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... when did Caern Rank have anything to do with what Gifts you can learn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going from WtA20, page 151 in the section Learning Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Traditionally, the Gaou first travels to a caern with a power level equal or greater than that of the desired Gift to petition the spirit personally - to do otherwise is to defy tradition, which risks incurring the wrath of the spirit.</b> </div> </div> </div>There is similar language in WtA Revised on page 132. It is also written in WtA 2nd Edition on page 114. I can't find such language in the first edition corebook though, but that is not surprising. First edition books always leave a lot of stuff out.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is not a rule too many people use!<br /> <br /> The game doesn't say it is an absolute requirement as Garou can do various things to cheat, fraud. or force such knowledge in other means, it is definitely not kosher. And it implies huge disfavor and animosity from the spirit world to those who violate this tradition. So perhaps I worded it too strongly without the appropriate caveats, but the level of the caern is supposed to be tied to the level of gift you can be taught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:02:15-07:00","id":939269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938737#post938737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoting wikipedia &quot;Casablanca is Morocco's chief <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port\" target=\"_blank\">port</a> and one of the largest <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_center\" target=\"_blank\">financial centers</a> on the African continent.&quot; and &quot;Casablanca is Morocco's chief <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port\" target=\"_blank\">port</a> and one of the largest <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_center\" target=\"_blank\">financial centers</a> on the African continent.&quot; Together with the port of Mohameddina 30km north, they perform 50% of the countrie's trade. Even in BC times, the city was influential for Phoenician and Roman sea travel. Having the mysterious Phat spirit housing his unique level 5 caern here, is okay, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still heavily disagree. Morocco still isn't a major trading crossroads. That its port is large for Africa (note Wikipedia doesn't even say it is the largest, just one of the largest) is meaningless. Casablanca isn't even in the Top 50 in the world. It certainly hasn't been the case historically. Casablanca was at the edge of the civilized world in antiquity. That it was a port doesn't mean it was a major port. Egypt was always the nexus of trade as it was connected to both the Mediterranean (and therefore Atlantic) and Red Sea (and therefore the Indian and Pacific). You only needed a portage to connect the two before the Suez Canal. Of course, you can't have a Silent Strider caern in Egypt.<br /> <br /> At best, I would make such a caern in Casablanca a Rank 3. Only if I saw a major mythical history in the caern description that adequately justified such power would I go with it. As I said, I'm fine not going on solely by real world history and geography. But if that doesn't justify it, then sell the idea to me.<br /> <br /> But we all have our different criteria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:05:58-07:00","id":939272,"title":"","content":"I think that statement is being taken a bit too strongly esp. with the rest of that paragraph and the following one. It's pretty clear that &quot;tradition&quot; is just that, tradition. It's not a requirement. The spirits might like tradition better, but between rolling well on Summoning, and simply being prepared with good chiminage to mollify the spirit's impending offense at going against tradition, it's pretty clear that Garou that don't have ready access to Rank 5 Caerns do just fine in getting Gifts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:08:24-07:00","id":939274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=938587#post938587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always figured places that scream &quot;rank 5 caern&quot; would be quickly bulldozed by the minions of the wyrm and turned into a tire factory; So keeping them on the &quot;DL&quot; very important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think this is a common problem for ANY Rank 5 caern. You can't exactly keep it on the down low to anyone who is spiritually sensitive. There is just too much power and spiritual traffic going on. And the books make this point saying that a major problem for such caerns is the need to defend them.<br /> <br /> I think rank 5 caerns were once common, but a lot have been lost. Those that survived must have some conditions that make it hard for Wyrm minions to successfully attack them.<br /> <br /> However, I don't think rank 5 caerns being at an appropriate place makes them any easier to detect to ones that aren't as obvious (to ignorant human eyes).<br /> <br /> I would have no problem if people posted ideas for historical rank 5 caerns that no longer exist along with the story of how they &quot;died&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T23:29:16-07:00","id":939374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939272#post939272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that statement is being taken a bit too strongly esp. with the rest of that paragraph and the following one. It's pretty clear that &quot;tradition&quot; is just that, tradition. It's not a requirement. The spirits might like tradition better, but between rolling well on Summoning, and simply being prepared with good chiminage to mollify the spirit's impending offense at going against tradition, it's pretty clear that Garou that don't have ready access to Rank 5 Caerns do just fine in getting Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the rulebooks doesn't say it is the only way, but it is the easiest, since all other ways require additional effort.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:33:36-07:00","id":939389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939269#post939269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still heavily disagree. Morocco still isn't a major trading crossroads. That its port is large for Africa (note Wikipedia doesn't even say it is the largest, just one of the largest) is meaningless. Casablanca isn't even in the Top 50 in the world. It certainly hasn't been the case historically. Casablanca was at the edge of the civilized world in antiquity. That it was a port doesn't mean it was a major port. Egypt was always the nexus of trade as it was connected to both the Mediterranean (and therefore Atlantic) and Red Sea (and therefore the Indian and Pacific). You only needed a portage to connect the two before the Suez Canal. Of course, you can't have a Silent Strider caern in Egypt.<br /> <br /> At best, I would make such a caern in Casablanca a Rank 3. Only if I saw a major mythical history in the caern description that adequately justified such power would I go with it. As I said, I'm fine not going on solely by real world history and geography. But if that doesn't justify it, then sell the idea to me.<br /> <br /> But we all have our different criteria.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet a God of Gates and Pathways decided to settle there. Ptah's judgement of relevance is the only benchmark relevant here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:54:42-07:00","id":939396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939389#post939389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet a God of Gates and Pathways decided to settle there. Ptah's judgement of relevance is the only benchmark relevant here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the spirit mentioned anywhere else, besides Nuwisha and this caern ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:08:41-07:00","id":939455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939396#post939396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the spirit mentioned anywhere else, besides Nuwisha and this caern ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage across Egypt, I think. Not sure if anywhere else, you're the one with encyclopedic knowledge of W:tA. Still, you can just crib stuff from the Egyptian mythology if you need to build him up further. Not that there aren't a million spirits that are named just once in W:tA.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:49:56-07:00","id":939468,"title":"","content":"Well, Followers of Set revised mentions the Egyptian demi-urge by that name as being responsible for the Ravnos Clan. Mummy resurrection has several mentiones, one as part of the trinity Ptah<br /> -Seker-Osiris as Creation-Stability-Death. Also father or Imopthep. 'Ptah's Word' allows a mummy to create an object instantly. 'Rage across Egypt' mentions a tribal Artefact 'Wheel of Ptah'. 'Nuwisha' also states that Ptah is the creator of the world and his followers are tasked with protecting other worlds/umbra parts from being integrated into the Weaver's web by the Void Engineers.<br /> <br /> With this background, Ptah is greater than Gaia and basically an all-mighty being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:44:29-07:00","id":939682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939129#post939129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much this.<br /> So for me, level 5 caerns should generally be far out of the way. I only use a handful of them in my games and they are always hard to get to and well protected.<br /> I'd say there are only about 1-3 level 5 Caerns per continent, if that. None are left on the east coast of the US since the human populations are too high and I've had them closed, destroyed or corrupted during the expansion west.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in a way that also cuts out a good chunk of the west coast too.. And on the west coast, you have a major issue with forest fires that can also ruin caerns..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:48:06-07:00","id":939720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939682#post939682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in a way that also cuts out a good chunk of the west coast too.. And on the west coast, you have a major issue with forest fires that can also ruin caerns..<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what the Caern is to. I could see a Caern located in under the forest being a Caern of healing or rebirth or destruction or Rage. There are a number of possibilities.<br /> <br /> I agree though. I think that if there are any, there are very few (maybe 1-2?) level 5 Caerns in the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:35:55-07:00","id":940161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939129#post939129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for me, level 5 caerns should generally be far out of the way. I only use a handful of them in my games and they are always hard to get to and well protected.<br /> I'd say there are only about 1-3 level 5 Caerns per continent, if that. None are left on the east coast of the US since the human populations are too high and I've had them closed, destroyed or corrupted during the expansion west.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is along my ways of thinking too. That would make it about 6-18 rank 5 caerns worldwide, not all of which are held by the Garou. This has implications to the setting I'll elaborate on in another post as not all tribes could control a Rank 5 by themselves.<br /> <br /> Europe might not even have any at all unless there is one in the Alps, northern Scandinavia, or perhaps an old urban caern that represents a strongly Weaver idea, and the city has represented that for a long time (likely only Paris and London have been old enough and successful enough to do that; I would add Rome but imagine it's been a stronghold of the Celestial Chorus and Istanbul has had too many declines and rises and declines to be rank 5).<br /> <br /> North America might actually have a few albeit mostly in northern Canada and Alaska, although the Rocky Mountain range in the US would also be good.<br /> <br /> Central and South America probably have a few places for them, but you're in areas outside the wolf range and likely held by Bastet or others.<br /> <br /> Same with Africa.<br /> <br /> Australia probably only has one. Rage Across Australia does not list any rank 5 caern that I can find so the ST is free to make up their own. The best place that comes to mind for it would be something like Uluru (Ayers Rock), but that is a place for a canonical Rank 4 caern.<br /> <br /> Asia is the largest continent and likely a place for more rank 5 caerns than any other. Besides the canonical rank 5 kingship caern held by the Silver Fangs, other bits of remote Siberia and Himalayas would make the most sense. This might be the only place whose rank 5 caerns are more than 3, but that will balance out some places with fewer. It also is the other continent with the best chance for a rank 5 urban caern. However, given how many cities rise and fall throughout history, it'd be hard for a city to have achieved rank 5 status and kept it to today. While the Levantine coast is a possible spot, I think China is the best region, especially Nanking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939129#post939129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The level 5 Strider Caern (the Wheel of Ptah) doesn't really both me so much. The idea of the Glasswalkers having a level 5 Caern is kind of an odd thought though to me. I never considered any inner city Caern to be that powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly be convinced of that. However, I think one of the world cities (alpha class or better) has the best chance. London, to me, is the only city with the longevity, power, culture, and strong emotional connection to one facet (as the financial capital of the world) to achieve rank 5 status. Probably happened in the late Victorian Era, and the city has struggled to keep it since the British Empire's decline.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:43:42-07:00","id":940167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=939389#post939389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet a God of Gates and Pathways decided to settle there. Ptah's judgement of relevance is the only benchmark relevant here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a certainly an acceptable answer in character for PCs and NPCs. However, I think it's a lame justification in real life. Especially since Morocco has no cultural connection to Ptah or the Egyptian Gods. This is a huge design flaw.<br /> <br /> To me, this needs a lot more work to justify to me. I'd even accept a location for the migration of animals (even birds and sea creatures off the coast, especially as a spot temporarily used along the migration route) to justify it, but as far as I know this part of Morocco isn't especially known for that (again, I'd be willing to accept a fictional depiction that it is, but the description needs to play that up). So it'd have to be something in the history of the sept, but I don't remember anything that did.<br /> <br /> I think Rank 5 caerns need to be very memorable (and more for just their power). The caern's powers are fine. It's just the location I find maddening.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:57:21-07:00","id":940172,"title":"","content":"If we assume a scenario where there are a dozen or less caerns controlled by the Garou around the world, this is something that drives the game setting because how you divide it up matters.<br /> <br /> While characters can find other ways to learn rank 5 gifts, they all pay a price for them. Not only does the extra chiminage begin to add up, if you learn more than one that way you are constantly angering the spirits. A neighbor might be willing to overlook one extremely annoying or offensive action with enough apologies and contrition, but if you keep doing the same thing such patience and forgiveness quickly changes no matter how contrite you seem at the moment. Now imagine if lots of your neighbors begin to do the same thing. You'd probably want to leave the neighborhood. This might have repercussions in the spirit world. Maybe one of the reasons Bone Gnawers don't have Pure Breed or Ancestors anymore is that the tribe was not given access to Rank 5 caerns, so any rank 5 elders had to go outside the system to do it, thus angering the spirits. After enough times and a long enough history, the spirits ended up responding and the resultant anger/pollution eroded their ability to contact Ancestors and killed their pure breed. Perhaps the Warders of Men were similar?<br /> <br /> So I think who holds Rank 5 caerns is important as it will be one of the things tribal (or possibly auspice) politics covers. A world which has each tribe jealousy guarding its own caern will leave some tribes out of luck (even if this is only used to emphasize how socially outcast the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers are). That is different than a world where there is one big multi-tribal Rank 5 caern that everyone has access to. Or maybe there is a particular caern strongly associated with one auspice, it is multi-tribal, but only for members of a certain auspice. So it is a tool for the ST on how he wants his tribal politics to be within the Nation.<br /> <br /> One reason I'd like to brainstorm ideas for Rank 5 caerns is so I know where to send the PCs once they get to that level. If they want to be allowed into that sept, they may want to visit them earlier in their careers, perform chiminage for them, and impress the Garou sept officers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:10:22-07:00","id":940179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940161#post940161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Australia probably only has one. Rage Across Australia does not list any rank 5 caern that I can find so the ST is free to make up their own. The best place that comes to mind for it would be something like Uluru (Ayers Rock), but that is a place for a canonical Rank 4 caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great Barrier Reef should be one. I think it's listed in the Apocalypse book if memory serves, and is &quot;controlled&quot; by the Rokea. Given real world events though it is probably dying unfortunately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940161#post940161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asia is the largest continent and likely a place for more rank 5 caerns than any other. Besides the canonical rank 5 kingship caern held by the Silver Fangs, other bits of remote Siberia and Himalayas would make the most sense. This might be the only place whose rank 5 caerns are more than 3, but that will balance out some places with fewer. It also is the other continent with the best chance for a rank 5 urban caern. However, given how many cities rise and fall throughout history, it'd be hard for a city to have achieved rank 5 status and kept it to today. While the Levantine coast is a possible spot, I think China is the best region, especially Nanking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the fall of a (the?) Stargazer Rank 5 Caern was the catalyst for them leaving the Garou nation. I would have thought that was located in the Himalayas, but its been a long time so I could be misremembering. I agree though that Asia should have more level 5 Caerns just based on the size of the continent. Admittedly I am not overly familiar with the geography of the continent so I wouldn't have any good guesses for where other might be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940161#post940161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can certainly be convinced of that. However, I think one of the world cities (alpha class or better) has the best chance. London, to me, is the only city with the longevity, power, culture, and strong emotional connection to one facet (as the financial capital of the world) to achieve rank 5 status. Probably happened in the late Victorian Era, and the city has struggled to keep it since the British Empire's decline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I could see that. Personally, I just like the idea of the Urrah Tribes (Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers) not having control of any of the Rank 5 Caerns in the world for story purposes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:24:12-07:00","id":940186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940172#post940172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While characters can find other ways to learn rank 5 gifts, they all pay a price for them. Not only does the extra chiminage begin to add up, if you learn more than one that way you are constantly angering the spirits. A neighbor might be willing to overlook one extremely annoying or offensive action with enough apologies and contrition, but if you keep doing the same thing such patience and forgiveness quickly changes no matter how contrite you seem at the moment. Now imagine if lots of your neighbors begin to do the same thing. You'd probably want to leave the neighborhood. This might have repercussions in the spirit world. Maybe one of the reasons Bone Gnawers don't have Pure Breed or Ancestors anymore is that the tribe was not given access to Rank 5 caerns, so any rank 5 elders had to go outside the system to do it, thus angering the spirits. After enough times and a long enough history, the spirits ended up responding and the resultant anger/pollution eroded their ability to contact Ancestors and killed their pure breed. Perhaps the Warders of Men were similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said earlier, this whole concept is new to me even after years of playing Werewolf. How I would look at it though is that while heading to a level 5 Caern is traditional for meeting spirits and learning Rank 5 Gifts on Earth, journeying to the Spirit's home realms would be just as acceptable. For some Rank 5 Gifts (the celestial ones) you kind of <i>have</i> to do that. I don't see a Garou summoning Rorg to the local level 5 Caern to have him teach them Gifts. And that's how I would have had rank 5 Bone Gnawers or Glasswalkers do it. They travel to Rat and Cockroach's respective realms. There also just aren't that many Rank 5 Garou, and even the ones that are written up in books don't usually have more than a few Rank 5 Gifts so making each gift harder to get doesn't bother me so much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940172#post940172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think who holds Rank 5 caerns is important as it will be one of the things tribal (or possibly auspice) politics covers. A world which has each tribe jealousy guarding its own caern will leave some tribes out of luck (even if this is only used to emphasize how socially outcast the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers are). That is different than a world where there is one big multi-tribal Rank 5 caern that everyone has access to. Or maybe there is a particular caern strongly associated with one auspice, it is multi-tribal, but only for members of a certain auspice. So it is a tool for the ST on how he wants his tribal politics to be within the Nation.<br /> <br /> One reason I'd like to brainstorm ideas for Rank 5 caerns is so I know where to send the PCs once they get to that level. If they want to be allowed into that sept, they may want to visit them earlier in their careers, perform chiminage for them, and impress the Garou sept officers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of the conflict this sets up. It also encourages higher rank Garou to journey the world and set up ties with a network of Caerns. That alone could explain some of why the Garou nation hasn't fractured more than it has.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:56:27-07:00","id":940201,"title":"","content":"While visiting spirits in the Umbra is certainly another option, the same section on Learning Gifts says it has its own perils. By saying it is tradition to do it this way, I assume &quot;tradition&quot; means this is how the spirits want it to be done. It might be the equivalent of visiting hours for a doctor or lawyer - do they want you to dropping by their office during their open hours, or do they want you coming to their home while they're eating dinner with their family?<br /> <br /> Of course, it's obvious a lot of players overlooked this in the corebook and are used to many years of gaming of where this wasn't done. It has a lot of impact of how the setting operates, so I understand why people will either continue to ignore it or adapt it so that it doesn't disrupt what they are used to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:03:03-07:00","id":940242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940201#post940201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While visiting spirits in the Umbra is certainly another option, the same section on Learning Gifts says it has its own perils. By saying it is tradition to do it this way, I assume &quot;tradition&quot; means this is how the spirits want it to be done. It might be the equivalent of visiting hours for a doctor or lawyer - do they want you to dropping by their office during their open hours, or do they want you coming to their home while they're eating dinner with their family?<br /> <br /> Of course, it's obvious a lot of players overlooked this in the corebook and are used to many years of gaming of where this wasn't done. It has a lot of impact of how the setting operates, so I understand why people will either continue to ignore it or adapt it so that it doesn't disrupt what they are used to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally saw the word traditional and thought that this was the most straight forward way that has been come up with over the eons. It's just how things are done now because it makes the most sense. The other changing breeds certainly don't have to visit level 5 Caerns to learn their gifts. So I feel it is more of an internal societal tradition.<br /> I actually like the idea though more and more as I think about it. I just think that spirit quests are an equally valid way to go about it. They are certainly not without their own complications admittedly. But what is the point of gaining rank if not to be able to handle some unexpectedness along the way. (for players I mean, obviously rank isn't about this in character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Elders essentially having to go on pilgrimages to various high level Caerns across the region in order to gain their powers. That benefits everyone insomuch as to become an Elder you kind of have to be known everywhere since you will have visited.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T23:24:32-07:00","id":940508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940161#post940161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is along my ways of thinking too. That would make it about 6-18 rank 5 caerns worldwide, not all of which are held by the Garou. This has implications to the setting I'll elaborate on in another post as not all tribes could control a Rank 5 by themselves.<br /> <br /> Europe might not even have any at all unless there is one in the Alps, northern Scandinavia, or perhaps an old urban caern that represents a strongly Weaver idea, and the city has represented that for a long time (likely only Paris and London have been old enough and successful enough to do that; I would add Rome but imagine it's been a stronghold of the Celestial Chorus and Istanbul has had too many declines and rises and declines to be rank 5).<br /> <br /> North America might actually have a few albeit mostly in northern Canada and Alaska, although the Rocky Mountain range in the US would also be good.<br /> <br /> Central and South America probably have a few places for them, but you're in areas outside the wolf range and likely held by Bastet or others.<br /> <br /> Same with Africa.<br /> <br /> Australia probably only has one. Rage Across Australia does not list any rank 5 caern that I can find so the ST is free to make up their own. The best place that comes to mind for it would be something like Uluru (Ayers Rock), but that is a place for a canonical Rank 4 caern.<br /> <br /> Asia is the largest continent and likely a place for more rank 5 caerns than any other. Besides the canonical rank 5 kingship caern held by the Silver Fangs, other bits of remote Siberia and Himalayas would make the most sense. This might be the only place whose rank 5 caerns are more than 3, but that will balance out some places with fewer. It also is the other continent with the best chance for a rank 5 urban caern. However, given how many cities rise and fall throughout history, it'd be hard for a city to have achieved rank 5 status and kept it to today. While the Levantine coast is a possible spot, I think China is the best region, especially Nanking.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my prior STs for Werewolf, had a list of where he had all 10 of the Rank five caerns he had placed.. 2 in South America, one in north, 1 in Canada, 2 in Asia, 1 in Europe, 1 in Africa.. His 10th, surprisingly was in the Indonesian island chains/borneo neck of the woods...Rokea controlled that one, but they would let others in...<br /> He felt that Australia was not strong enough to warrant a RK 5 one, since the most powerful WAS the Ayers rock locale.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940179#post940179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the fall of a (the?) Stargazer Rank 5 Caern was the catalyst for them leaving the Garou nation. I would have thought that was located in the Himalayas, but its been a long time so I could be misremembering. I agree though that Asia should have more level 5 Caerns just based on the size of the continent. Admittedly I am not overly familiar with the geography of the continent so I wouldn't have any good guesses for where other might be</div> </div> </div> </div>That it was.. Which was NOT one of the 2 he had listed, as his games were always set around just AFTER the Gazers left to go join the beast courts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T00:41:20-07:00","id":940521,"title":"","content":"The number of responses is still low, but there seems to be an early consensus that Rank 5 caerns maybe number between 6-18. Ten is right smack dab in the middle. I prefer a low number myself, but in canon the numbers appear to be much higher. So I expected players to come in with a much higher number. I'm glad to see people are placing it more in the range I expected, even lower to be honest.<br /> <br /> Maybe we can begin taking one continent at a time and brainstorm what areas and types make sense for them. Europe tends to be a well known continent, and the places are fairly limited (likely the Alps and/or northern Scandinavia since they are the least populated) so let's start there. Given the location, it seems likely the Get of Fenris would be important in the sept. Anything else we can add?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:50:13-07:00","id":940574,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem with how many there &quot;should&quot; be is that the books are pretty inconsistent about Caern level rarity (or even what really what's the most important factor as to why it should be ranked what it is).<br /> <br /> I feel like there's a strong disconnect here because there's an assumption in the thread that level 5 Caerns only happen in uniquely special places... but the books don't really say that. Caern level is usually a matter of effort by Garou to build up the spiritual power of the Caern and its Totem. That's why large Septs go hand-in-hand with high power Caerns. Even without the defense needed that those numbers represent, you need a larger number of Garou (and kin) maintaining the Caern to keep it potent.<br /> <br /> Just focusing on Caerns that seem to naturally/symbolically make sense to be natural wellsprings of power makes sense for the small numbers being talked about. Including Caerns that are highly ranked by virtue of a few generations of plan old hard work should expand that number significantly. The Sept of the Green is less than 200 years old, and it's Caern with it, but so much effort's gone into it that NYC's biggest Sept has a very potent Caern in that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T07:03:28-07:00","id":940608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940508#post940508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of my prior STs for Werewolf, had a list of where he had all 10 of the Rank five caerns he had placed.. 2 in South America, one in north, 1 in Canada, 2 in Asia, 1 in Europe, 1 in Africa.. His 10th, surprisingly was in the Indonesian island chains/borneo neck of the woods...Rokea controlled that one, but they would let others in...<br /> He felt that Australia was not strong enough to warrant a RK 5 one, since the most powerful WAS the Ayers rock locale..</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be picky, but you listed 9, and it's interesting to see that there is 1 in North America <i>and</i> 1 in Canada? For Australia, for me, I would've put one on Ayers Rock (now gone) and The Great Barrier Reef should still be one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940574#post940574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the problem with how many there &quot;should&quot; be is that the books are pretty inconsistent about Caern level rarity (or even what really what's the most important factor as to why it should be ranked what it is).<br /> <br /> I feel like there's a strong disconnect here because there's an assumption in the thread that level 5 Caerns only happen in uniquely special places... but the books don't really say that. Caern level is usually a matter of effort by Garou to build up the spiritual power of the Caern and its Totem. That's why large Septs go hand-in-hand with high power Caerns. Even without the defense needed that those numbers represent, you need a larger number of Garou (and kin) maintaining the Caern to keep it potent.<br /> <br /> Just focusing on Caerns that seem to naturally/symbolically make sense to be natural wellsprings of power makes sense for the small numbers being talked about. Including Caerns that are highly ranked by virtue of a few generations of plan old hard work should expand that number significantly. The Sept of the Green is less than 200 years old, and it's Caern with it, but so much effort's gone into it that NYC's biggest Sept has a very potent Caern in that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is how I've always viewed it (and it doesn't necessarily have to be backed up by the books) for my games. I see Caern power levels as generally only sliding downwards. It takes an epic event or story to actually increase the level of a Caern. So most level 5 Caerns had to have started out in a place that warrant it being a level 5 Caern and then have been maintained over the course of eons. I would allow a level 4 Caern to be raised up to a level 5, but whatever lead to that happening would be the kind of stuff every Garou talks about and knows. I used to use Sept of the Green a lot (l lived in NY for a long time and all of my players were familiar with the area and landmarks) and I had the Sept start at level 1 or 2. All of the effort put in to carve Central Park out of the expanding city and maintaining the area/forest, <u>and</u> the bringing in of an additional Caern Totem (practically unheard of) ended up raising it up to where it is now (Level 3). I had a fairly in depth history written out for the Caern and city and that explained why the Caern was 1 to 2 levels above what it should have been (again, for my games).<br /> Using this format though, it would take exponential effort to raise a Caern each additional level. A Caern going up 1 level could happen over the course of an entire Chronicle. Going up another level should happen because of the efforts of several generations of Garou, and even then it wouldn't be guaranteed by any means. All of this has to happen with the world sliding towards Apocalypse, so in general it's taking more and more effort to just maintain the Caern levels where they're at already. This is how I normally view/run Caern levels for my own games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 07-31-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T07:21:09-07:00","id":940614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940521#post940521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we can begin taking one continent at a time and brainstorm what areas and types make sense for them. Europe tends to be a well known continent, and the places are fairly limited (likely the Alps and/or northern Scandinavia since they are the least populated) so let's start there. Given the location, it seems likely the Get of Fenris would be important in the sept. Anything else we can add?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Europe, I like the idea of the Get and the Fianna both having level 5 Caerns. Sept of the Tri Spiral works adequately for me, though I tend to view it as a mix of how it's written up in Caerns: Places of Power and how the Hidden Halls of Edinburgh are written up in the Dresden Files.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:21:03-07:00","id":940743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940608#post940608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be picky, but you listed 9, and it's interesting to see that there is 1 in North America <i>and</i> 1 in Canada? For Australia, for me, I would've put one on Ayers Rock (now gone) and The Great Barrier Reef should still be one.</div> </div> </div> </div>DOH.. If i remember rightly, i think his 10th, was maybe in the ice/greenland neck of the woods...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:42:20-07:00","id":940757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940608#post940608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is how I've always viewed it (and it doesn't necessarily have to be backed up by the books) for my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that, but it is ultimately not helpful for a conversation.<br /> <br /> Either (1) participants are entering an echo chamber because everyone contributing is on one page and everyone's ignoring all the valid things that come from other approaches, or (2) multiple views on how things &quot;should&quot; be just hit loggerheads because ultimately nobody is right about how things &quot;should&quot; be in their own games. <br /> <br /> One of the reasons why so many RPG discussions get so invested on &quot;what the book says,&quot; is because the whole point of the books is to be a common base-line for everyone to agree on as the starting point. <br /> <br /> If we completely toss out the books-as-base-line, then you have your thing, and I have my thing, and... how do we move on to something constructive about who many Rank 5 Caerns there &quot;should&quot; be and where they should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:40:27-07:00","id":940818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940757#post940757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate that, but it is ultimately not helpful for a conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. This conversation has been fairly helpful and interesting for me at least, and I would hope to the others involved as well. When posting on here, I try and make sure to caveat statements that I make with references for where the information came from that way there isn't a misunderstanding. Sometimes I'm typing with books open in front of me, most the time with information from memory and sometimes with houserules or storylines that divert from canon. I am making sure to specify which sometimes to attempt to keep misunderstanding to a minimum.<br /> <br /> Thank you though for the implication that input was not wanted on your statements. I will try to avoid doing so again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T00:29:24-07:00","id":941082,"title":"","content":"I don't have Caerns: Places of Power in front of me. Is the Sept of the Tri-Spiral a Rank 5 caern? That is supposed to be the big Werewolf-Chanegeling crossover spot, right? I have no problem with such a caern. Give me a good enough description and history, and I'll accept a lot. Since Fae are fictional anyway, a related caern will rely more on fiction than real world features.<br /> <br /> Still trying to figure out a good spot for a Rank 5 caern in Scandinavia and possibly the Alps.<br /> <br /> I think at one point the Brocken in the Harz mountains of Germany, home to many witch legends, was a Rank 5 caern. But I think it would have been reduced as the area became more familiar in the 19th and 20th centuries. Still possibly a Rank 4 caern.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is the Bialowieza Forest in Poland/Belarus. It is one of the last primeval forest in Europe and last remaining spot for the European Bison. I can see the Silver Fangs being camped out there with possibly some other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T01:44:37-07:00","id":941101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=940167#post940167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a certainly an acceptable answer in character for PCs and NPCs. However, I think it's a lame justification in real life. Especially since Morocco has no cultural connection to Ptah or the Egyptian Gods. This is a huge design flaw.<br /> <br /> To me, this needs a lot more work to justify to me. I'd even accept a location for the migration of animals (even birds and sea creatures off the coast, especially as a spot temporarily used along the migration route) to justify it, but as far as I know this part of Morocco isn't especially known for that (again, I'd be willing to accept a fictional depiction that it is, but the description needs to play that up). So it'd have to be something in the history of the sept, but I don't remember anything that did.<br /> <br /> I think Rank 5 caerns need to be very memorable (and more for just their power). The caern's powers are fine. It's just the location I find maddening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's one of those things where you need to disconnect your bullshit meter. Most of the biggest and most powerful Caerns were placed during the early years of White Wolf. We all know that they sucked on the topics of geopolitics, history and geography and considered stereotypes to be a perfectly valid analysys of how a culture works. Caerns pop up in random places where there is a confluence of gnosis and shallowings in the Umbra, in setting they can be anywhere. So just because they're not in the most thematically appropriate place, doesn't mean that they couldn't be there anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T03:03:31-07:00","id":941118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=941101#post941101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]considered stereotypes to be a perfectly valid analysis of how a culture works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stereotypes can be a perfectly valid thought about specific types of individuals or certain ways of doing things. They don't have to be fact, but they can be. Point is, stereotype isn't a bad thing. It makes the world accessible and they have had their place in inter-cultural relations since forever. Also, there is usually a trigger that made a group of people think that another group had a certain quality that was characteristic, therefore starting the stereotype. So, most stereotypes are still based on some observation that while not necessarily absolute correct or applicable every member of the target group is still a valid observation.<br /> <br /> That said, true, a lot of Werewolf 1st Edition is messy like that, but I find revised or W20s attempts to correct is even more annoying. Forsaken was designed to not have (that much) messed up setting elements, there was no need to remove them from revised and W20 and make an even bigger mess.<br /> <br /> Also, I didn't even think to much about Phat, didn't know he was a egyptian god, and hadn't remembered him from Nuwisha, until I re-read it recently. So, I thought it was just one unique spirit on one unique caern and that was fine with me. While not a big city and not the most prominent one in all of history, Anfa/Casa Blanca has a certain allure and I didn't ever think it would be unworthy for a high level caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T11:27:08-07:00","id":941286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=941082#post941082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't have Caerns: Places of Power in front of me. Is the Sept of the Tri-Spiral a Rank 5 caern? That is supposed to be the big Werewolf-Chanegeling crossover spot, right? I have no problem with such a caern. Give me a good enough description and history, and I'll accept a lot. Since Fae are fictional anyway, a related caern will rely more on fiction than real world features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it is (a level 5 Caern). I was surprised when I looked it up. So that's the one I normally default to when thinking of the Fianna. Like I said, though for my games I change it a bit. I haven't had players actually go there though, so that's less important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=941082#post941082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still trying to figure out a good spot for a Rank 5 caern in Scandinavia and possibly the Alps.<br /> <br /> I think at one point the Brocken in the Harz mountains of Germany, home to many witch legends, was a Rank 5 caern. But I think it would have been reduced as the area became more familiar in the 19th and 20th centuries. Still possibly a Rank 4 caern.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is the Bialowieza Forest in Poland/Belarus. It is one of the last primeval forest in Europe and last remaining spot for the European Bison. I can see the Silver Fangs being camped out there with possibly some other tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I like the idea of the Bialowieza Forest over a random spot in the Alps. It might be a bit far east for Get domination though so that would leave tribal makeup more up in the air. Until I saw where it was on the map I was thinking Get/Talon. Not sure what direction I would go with on the Caern Spirit either. <br /> <br /> In my mind, especially with the older or more powerful Caerns I view them as being predominantly one tribe, maybe 2. I don't see many of the older Caerns being multi-tribal. The books though don't always agree with this (consistency again), but I would guess that more has to do with the writers wanting them to be more inclusive sometimes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:17:12-07:00","id":941604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=941101#post941101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's one of those things where you need to disconnect your bullshit meter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could do that, but I'd rather just eliminate the caern in my chronicle and move on. I wouldn't be bothered by it if I was playing in someone else's chronicle who used it for the reasons you indicated. I always take a very ala carte approach to anything not in the corebook. There is lots of good stuff and lots of dreck so I pick and choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-03-2016, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:28:42-07:00","id":941612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=941286#post941286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my mind, especially with the older or more powerful Caerns I view them as being predominantly one tribe, maybe 2. I don't see many of the older Caerns being multi-tribal. The books though don't always agree with this (consistency again), but I would guess that more has to do with the writers wanting them to be more inclusive sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a major issue with septs and their tribal make up is that everything indicates a single tribe, or a very small number of tribes, but the game's character creation emphasizes multi-tribal PC packs (because players want to pick whatever) so supplements are written with that in mind.<br /> <br /> I'm personally inclined to mono-tribal Rank 5 septs, or very limited number of tribes. As an ST, I think that creates a lot of tribal politics which is a good thing. At the same time, I also understand that its easiest on the ST and PCs to detail only one rank 5 caern where all PC tribes can go to. It really depends on what kind of game and setting the ST wants to create. Of course, there will be so many game sessions before &quot;needing&quot; a rank 5 caern comes into play so that it may be moot.<br /> <br /> But the game definitely changes if the Uktena and Wendigo each have the only rank 5 caerns in North America. To each having one and third tribe also have one (say the Red Talons). Or that the Uktena and Wendigo share a Rank 5 caern, and the only other one held is held by an alliance of the other Garou tribes lead by one of the Silver Fang Houses, or that it is held by pseduo-hippie Children of Gaia who welcome everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:19:46-07:00","id":942103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=941612#post941612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a major issue with septs and their tribal make up is that everything indicates a single tribe, or a very small number of tribes, but the game's character creation emphasizes multi-tribal PC packs (because players want to pick whatever) so supplements are written with that in mind.<br /> <br /> I'm personally inclined to mono-tribal Rank 5 septs, or very limited number of tribes. As an ST, I think that creates a lot of tribal politics which is a good thing. At the same time, I also understand that its easiest on the ST and PCs to detail only one rank 5 caern where all PC tribes can go to. It really depends on what kind of game and setting the ST wants to create. Of course, there will be so many game sessions before &quot;needing&quot; a rank 5 caern comes into play so that it may be moot.<br /> <br /> But the game definitely changes if the Uktena and Wendigo each have the only rank 5 caerns in North America. To each having one and third tribe also have one (say the Red Talons). Or that the Uktena and Wendigo share a Rank 5 caern, and the only other one held is held by an alliance of the other Garou tribes lead by one of the Silver Fang Houses, or that it is held by pseduo-hippie Children of Gaia who welcome everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why i prefer it if the LOWER ranked Caerns are more those which are 'open to all', and the higher up in rank of the Caern, the more it goes to just one tribe (or in some cases more to one shifter)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:03:53-07:00","id":942136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=942103#post942103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why i prefer it if the LOWER ranked Caerns are more those which are 'open to all', and the higher up in rank of the Caern, the more it goes to just one tribe (or in some cases more to one shifter)..</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I usually run things. I think I've only ever had 1 game where the group was from a higher level Caern (4), but that was a period Hengeyokai game so there was plenty of character diversity to be had. In all other games (more traditional Werewolf games), the group was from a level 2 or 3 Caern. It's low enough to allow for more tribal variation in my mind, but high enough to have enough internal politics to deal with and plenty of inter-Sept politics for the group as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:32:07-07:00","id":945066,"title":"","content":"Most rank 1 caerns likely only have 1-3 packs at most (and if 3 packs, those are very small packs). It's probable that they are mono-tribal, or perhaps two closely allied tribes (Uktena and Wendigo, Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers, Silver Fangs plus a flunky, or some other understandable combination (such as Fianna and Get of Fenris considering the overlap between between Celtic and Germanic peoples over the centuries.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about Rank 1 caerns, is that you can place them almost anywhere and keep the Garou population low. Very easy to introduce new NPCs that way.<br /> <br /> Rank 2-4 caerns I can see as multi-tribal (or at least closely allied tribes), but certainly not all of them. The canonical Sept of the Green in New York has to be one of the more diverse multi-tribal septs, and is probably a legacy of New York being the traditional entry port for immigrants into the United States. I imagine most multi-tribal septs are limited to 4-6 tribes, and many of those tribes are probably those you would expect to be part of multi-tribe septs - Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, and Silver Fangs plus travelers like Silent Striders, Stargazers, and Black Furies.<br /> <br /> I think large multi-tribal septs - those having 10 tribes or more let's say - are extremely rare.<br /> <br /> Of course, there is a tradition of young Garou being Anruth and travelling from sept to sept. I think certain kinds of caerns are probably known to welcome them. It's hard for me to say those caerns are &quot;multi-tribal&quot; as anruth packs do not stay long, but certainly it is another way to introduce some variety into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:45:40-07:00","id":945073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=941286#post941286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I like the idea of the Bialowieza Forest over a random spot in the Alps</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bialowieza has an obvious hook, but I don't think an alpine caern should be dismissed as some &quot;random spot&quot;. There are lots of cool things about the alps. First, they are majestic and beautiful, or at least striking. You can find some great images of all kinds of mountains that would make great backdrops to a caern. Second, there are glaciers there going back to the Ice Ages.<br /> Third, they are the source for the major rivers and watersheds in Europe - both the Rhine and Danube begin there. Fourth, they also offer a diverse range of habitat in a small area because of the differences in heights.<br /> <br /> The decentralized political structure of Switzerland, and that the alps cover several countries, means an ST has lots of ways to explain why a particular corner of the Alps can be controlled by Garou and perhaps their kinfolk make up most of the local population as well.<br /> <br /> I think it would be very easy to craft some kind of story behind an impressive rank 5 caern here with lots of different caern types as options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:59:05-07:00","id":945078,"title":"","content":"The best place to put a Scandinavian rank 5 caern is somewhere in the north, most likely around the northern Scandinavian mountains, north of the arctic circle. This far north, many of the inhabitants aren't even Germanic Norwegians or Swedes, but Lapplanders (Sami). I think that makes it interesting for the Get. Lots of different climate zones here. While I don't know enough to place it in any one spectacular spot, I like the idea of it being tied to the reindeer migrations, and the reindeer is most likely the totem.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps as a result of its location north of the arctic circle, it was particularly associated with the pole star or aurora borealis.<br /> <br /> I imagine that way long ago when caerns were more numerous, this particular rank 5 caern was not seen as especially important compared to others. But as the other caerns declined and became reduced in number, this correspondingly became more and more important, and is not extremely revered among the Get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:08:48-07:00","id":945197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=945078#post945078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best place to put a Scandinavian rank 5 caern is somewhere in the north, most likely around the northern Scandinavian mountains, north of the arctic circle. This far north, many of the inhabitants aren't even Germanic Norwegians or Swedes, but Lapplanders (Sami). I think that makes it interesting for the Get. Lots of different climate zones here. While I don't know enough to place it in any one spectacular spot, I like the idea of it being tied to the reindeer migrations, and the reindeer is most likely the totem.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps as a result of its location north of the arctic circle, it was particularly associated with the pole star or aurora borealis.<br /> <br /> I imagine that way long ago when caerns were more numerous, this particular rank 5 caern was not seen as especially important compared to others. But as the other caerns declined and became reduced in number, this correspondingly became more and more important, and is not extremely revered among the Get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it.<br /> And from there you can have level 4 Caerns in the Alps and in the forest, still quite powerful, but lesser in comparison. So for Europe the remaining levels 5s could be the Tri-Spiral (Fianna) and northern Scandinavian (Get).<br /> <br /> I do think around the world each Tribe should at least have access to a level 5 Caern. The 3 tribes I see as having the most trouble might be the Gnawers, Glasswalker and maybe the Striders (having maybe lost theirs in Egypt) if you don't like the Wheel of Ptah.<br /> Having gone back and read through the Wheel of Ptah, the Caern is directly powered by the Incarna Ptah and the Caern center is a temple consecrated to him/it. So the reason given for it's location is basically Incarna level hand waving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T22:17:38-07:00","id":945293,"title":"","content":"I definitely don't see the Bone Gnawers controlling a level 5 caern (neither alone, nor as one of the major tribes in a multi-tribe sept). Individuals may get access to one, but over all the tribe suffers from its omega status.<br /> <br /> We've covered Europe, so North America is the next place. Most players will be familiar with it so it'll be easy. Then we can hit the other continents where people's knowledge is likely less.<br /> <br /> The level 5 caerns will likely be in Canada or Alaska, although the Rockies in the US is also likely. Obviously the most likely tribes to control them here are Wendigo and Uktena. A Wendigo caern in Canada is an obvious choice. The Uktena will be harder as their hunting grounds - Mexico and the southern US - aren't the most likely spots. I wonder if that means they'll be a caern that is shared between the Uktena and Wendigo. That would be interesting for one of the least populated/powerful tribes to have access to two caerns. If it is multi-tribal and we don't think they're powerful enough to hold it, then maybe we can throw in the Children of Gaia as well. I'll have to think of that.<br /> <br /> Red Talons holding a caern in northern Canada or Alaska is also possible (if not here, then it'll have to be in Siberia in Asia).<br /> <br /> Another possibility is a huge multi-sept caern of European descended Garou likely lead by one of the Silver Fang royal houses, perhaps Unbreakable Hearth. That would likely put them in the middle of Canada, say Saskatchewan or Alberta.<br /> <br /> I'll have to do some reading to see what locations, events, or stories I like that inspire me. Suggestions are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:51:35-07:00","id":945456,"title":"","content":"Haven't looked anything up yet, but I do like the idea of a Wendigo Caern up north and an Uktena Caern located in Central America/Mexico.<br /> Actually, given Mexico's in game Spiral problem, I wouldn't mind if their biggest caern was turned into a hive, leaving them with just being able to use the Wendigo's due to tribal alliances. And then a maybe a Caern somewhere in the Rockies that is Child of Gaia dominant, but open to visitors. I don't know where else in the World a CoG caern would be placed, so this seems like as good a choice as any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:29:54-07:00","id":945880,"title":"","content":"I'm leery of a Mexican rank 5 caern only because most of the <a href=\"http://www.azgfd.gov/i_e/ee/lessons/wolves/intro.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Mexican gray wolf range</a> was noticeably north of the main Meso-American civilizations, and the wolf was never in Central America. I don't see the Uktena holding onto anything there unless there was a good spot in northern Mexico for it. If one exists, I think it would most likely be held by the Balam as the <a href=\"https://news.mongabay.com/2012/09/jaguar-conservation-gets-a-boost-in-north-and-central-america/\" target=\"_blank\">jaguar's historical range</a> covers most of that territory. However, there might be some good potential sites in the Sierra Madre Occidental. I live in Arizona and am particularly found of the Madrean Sky Islands as a site of a caern. The Sonoran Desert that straddles the US and Mexico is the wettest desert in the world. I think there are lots of cool places - I'm just suspect that any of them are truly worthy of being rank 5. But I am open to the idea. I just need to be convinced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:54:03-07:00","id":946480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=945880#post945880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm leery of a Mexican rank 5 caern only because most of the <a href=\"http://www.azgfd.gov/i_e/ee/lessons/wolves/intro.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Mexican gray wolf range</a> was noticeably north of the main Meso-American civilizations, and the wolf was never in Central America. I don't see the Uktena holding onto anything there unless there was a good spot in northern Mexico for it. If one exists, I think it would most likely be held by the Balam as the <a href=\"https://news.mongabay.com/2012/09/jaguar-conservation-gets-a-boost-in-north-and-central-america/\" target=\"_blank\">jaguar's historical range</a> covers most of that territory. However, there might be some good potential sites in the Sierra Madre Occidental. I live in Arizona and am particularly found of the Madrean Sky Islands as a site of a caern. The Sonoran Desert that straddles the US and Mexico is the wettest desert in the world. I think there are lots of cool places - I'm just suspect that any of them are truly worthy of being rank 5. But I am open to the idea. I just need to be convinced.</div> </div> </div> </div>And with the large cartel presence through out Mexico IRL&lt; i would hate to see how much worse it would be in a WoD setting! So i agree, i just can't see enough land available to have created a Rk 5 caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:39:10-07:00","id":946517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns?p=946480#post946480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And with the large cartel presence through out Mexico IRL&lt; i would hate to see how much worse it would be in a WoD setting! So i agree, i just can't see enough land available to have created a Rk 5 caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I was suggesting that there <i>was</i> a level 5 caern there which may or may not be a level 5 hive now. I think it would be rather fitting given how Mexico is described as overrun by Spirals in the WoD. That would leave the Uktena having to head all the way up north to the Wendigo Caern to learn their rank 5 gifts, or possibly going to a lone remaining US level 5 Caern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}